From dff001ee531d74abf698d90cc7c3f0915d4f35ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:37:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Program: capacity jobs fed from workstream 10's lots
 (capacity + custody) [skip ci]

DepositToJob gains a source (frontier_abi::capacity: SOURCE_VAULT, the
user's own vault, or SOURCE_LOT, another owner's lot under its use order
for the user with purpose 0x0901). In a build with both previews the
lot's vault must be in the facility's province (the owner's decision of
2026-11-06: same province is direct use), the job's deposit and the
lot's use are one instruction: the rules record the deposit once
(resends change nothing), workstream 10's kernel consumes the whole
units under the order, and the lot's own LOT_CONSUMED record is logged
on its chain as ConsumeLot logs it. A job account keeps a link (which
lot, taken, returned, owed). A job takes each input from one source:
the user's own ore into a lot-fed job, or a second lot, is the mixed
case, undecided, refused (NotImplemented).

ClaimJob of a lot-fed job (the lot and its vault listed after the
user's vault) follows the owner's decisions: the products and the
user's wood go to the user's vault, the ore the job did not use goes
back into the lot un-consumed (workstream 10's return_unused, whole
units); a sub-unit rest, or what a frozen or full lot cannot take,
stays owed in the job and a later ClaimJob pays it; RetireJob refuses a
job that still owes. No record is logged for the return (workstream 10
has no record kind for return_unused yet; asked). A build without
custody refuses a lot source as unknown data.

Host tests (no key generated, derived or signed): 31 ore from M's lot in
A's vault and B's own wood make 15.25 arms; B gets the arms and its
wood, none of the lot's ore; the 0.5 ore left is owed and the job
cannot retire; not-whole units are refused by workstream 10's kernel; a
resend does not consume twice; B's own ore into the job is refused; in
a second run the one whole unit left goes back un-consumed and the job
retires.

Tests: permutation-frontier 107 default, 111 capacity-preview, 108
custody-preview, 114 both; frontier-abi 152 with the feature; clippy
-D warnings in all four builds; fmt. SBF, LiteSVM, the verifier's
tests not run.

